On Mon, 2007-11-12 at 17:35 +0100, Rafael Garcia-Suarez wrote:
> Here's a list of dual-lived modules in the core that have patches that
> aren't yet integrated in the CPAN version. It would be nice to release
> versions on CPAN with those changes in, in order to distribute perl
> 5.10 with "authorized" versions of core modules.
> 
> We've already delayed too much the release of 5.10, so, with the
> exception of the latest syncs to Jos' modules, (a security fix to
> Archive::Tar and a warning fix in CPANPLUS::Dist::Build), I'd like to
> stop accepting code patches now, except the ones that bump $VERSION
> variables to non-alpha version numbers. VMS portability will be
> achieved later. The general opinion is that File::Spec really needs
> some rewrite (or replacement) here.
> 
> Note that it's not important that you actually release a version of
> your dual life module to CPAN, just make sure that if you release one
> with the same version number as what comes with the core, both
> versions match. In other words, it's sufficient to "burn" a version
> number for the 5.10 core to use.

I think the patch taking Term::Cap to the version on CPAN got missed a
